  </div></header>
  <main>
    <section class="hero hero-video"><video class="bgvid" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster="/img/russ/v2/home-room-poster.jpg"><source src="/img/russ/v2/home-room.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video><div class="veil"></div>
      <div class="wrap hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Russ Michaels · Speaking</p>
        <h1>A human <em>on the podium.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Russ speaks on listening, judgment and what stays human as the machines get brilliant. An attorney, a twenty-year operator, and a coach who has stood in the rooms where people decide what their lives are for.</p>
        <div class="ctarow"><a class="btn btn-acc" href="#book">Book Russ</a><a class="btn btn-line" href="#topics">See the topics</a></div>
      </div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec" id="offers"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Russ offers</p><h2>Keynotes and rooms.</h2></div>
      <ul class="sp-offers"><li>Keynotes</li><li>Moderated conversations</li><li>Workshops</li><li>Fireside chats</li><li>Leadership offsites</li><li>Guided practices</li></ul>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec gallery-sec"><div class="wrap"><p class="strip-head">On stage and in the room</p><div class="gallery">
      <figure><img src="/img/russ/v2/home-mic.jpg" alt="Russ speaking with a microphone on a lit stage" style="object-position:50% 28%" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Keynotes</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/russ/v2/home-marianne.jpg" alt="Russ on stage with a microphone beside Marianne Williamson" style="object-position:100% 30%" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Conversations</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/img/russ/v2/learned-whiteboard.jpg" alt="Russ teaching in front of a whiteboard drawing of the 360" style="object-position:50% 50%" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Workshops</figcaption></figure>
    </div></div></section>

    <section class="sec alt" id="topics"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Most requested</p><h2>Topics.</h2><p class="lede">Every talk is built for your room and your people. Two tracks: the human work of listening, trust and change, and the human side of the machines now in every meeting.</p></div>
      <div class="sp-tracks"><h3 class="sp-track">The human work</h3><ol class="sp-topics"><li><h3>The Listening Loop</h3><p>Listen. Hear. Discern. Create. Most teams don’t have a communication problem; they have a listening problem. This is the four-step loop under every Vault Human program, taught so people use it on Monday.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>In the room: pairs run the loop on a real decision, out loud.</span><span>They leave with: one loop for meetings, one-on-ones and hard conversations.</span></p></li><li><h3>Trust is a daily deposit</h3><p>Trust isn’t built at the offsite. It’s built in small promises kept, and quietly spent when they aren’t. A talk about the account every team is already keeping.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>In the room: the team names where trust was earned and where it was spent this month.</span><span>They leave with: a shared language for repair and one daily habit.</span></p></li><li><h3>Yours, or inherited?</h3><p>How we lead, argue and rest came from somewhere: a parent, a first boss, a hard year. A look at which habits we chose and which we simply carried in.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>In the room: each person sorts three of their own defaults into keep, change and let go.</span><span>They leave with: one habit chosen on purpose.</span></p></li><li><h3>One small thing a day</h3><p>Big change rarely holds. Small change, done daily, does. Why the smallest practice beats the biggest plan, and how to build one that outlasts the event.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>In the room: everyone designs a thirty-day practice before they leave their seat.</span><span>They leave with: the practice, and a way to keep it.</span></p></li><li><h3>Who sings the “we”?</h3><p>Forty voices, one song. What a 1985 recording session teaches about teams, ego and keeping the human part in the room.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>In the room: the team writes its own “we” line together.</span><span>They leave with: a picture of the team at its best, and what it asks of each person.</span></p></li><li><h3>Law, life, legacy: one house</h3><p>Why the help we get comes in pieces, and how families and companies put it back together.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>Best for: family businesses, advisors, boards and anyone planning a handoff.</span><span>They leave with: one map of the decisions that belong in the same conversation.</span></p></li></ol><h3 class="sp-track">The human side of AI</h3><ol class="sp-topics"><li><h3>Let AI get brilliant. Let us get wiser.</h3><p>The machines are getting smarter every month. The question is whether we are. A keynote on judgment, attention and the parts of a life that should never be automated.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>Best for: all-hands, conferences and leadership kickoffs.</span><span>They leave with: three questions to ask before handing any decision to a tool.</span></p></li><li><h3>Whose choice was it?</h3><p>Estate law has a test for decisions that are yours in name only. Russ runs it, live, on the AI tools your people already use.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>In the room: the audience scores a real AI-assisted decision together.</span><span>They leave with: a five-minute test for any decision that matters.</span></p></li><li><h3>Hand on the key</h3><p>Leading when your tools act on their own: who checks the math, who owns the off switch, and who takes the stick when it matters.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>Best for: boards, executive teams, risk and operations leaders.</span><span>They leave with: a named owner for every switch that matters.</span></p></li><li><h3>The films that saw it coming</h3><p>WarGames, 2001, Electric Dreams. Classic movies, current headlines, and what they ask of us now.</p><p class="sp-meta"><span>Best for: conferences, evening events and client gatherings.</span><span>They leave with: a story worth retelling, and the question under it.</span></p></li></ol></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec" id="fees"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Fees</p><h2>Three ways to bring Russ in.</h2><p class="lede">Every engagement starts with a short planning call with your team, so the talk fits your room.</p></div>
      <div class="sp-fees">
        <div class="sp-fee"><h3>Keynote</h3><div class="price"><small>from</small> $5,000</div><p>45 to 60 minutes, built for your audience, with a planning call beforehand.</p></div>
        <div class="sp-fee sp-fee--main"><span class="sp-badge">Most requested</span><h3>Keynote + workshop</h3><div class="price"><small>from</small> $12,500</div><p>The talk, then the room puts it to work. A keynote followed by a half-day session with your people.</p></div>
        <div class="sp-fee"><h3>Workshop</h3><div class="price"><small>from</small> $6,000</div><p>Ninety minutes to a full day, hands-on, with practices your people keep using.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="offers-note">Fees shown are for live events. Virtual sessions, panels and fireside conversations, travel and recording rights are quoted with your date. A few community-rate engagements are held each year for nonprofits and aligned groups.</p>
      <div class="ctarow" style="margin-top:26px"><a class="btn btn-acc" href="#book">Check Russ’s availability</a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec alt" id="book"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Book Russ</p><h2>Tell us about your event.</h2><p class="lede">Share as much as you can. Russ reads every request and answers within two business days.</p></div>
      <form class="sp-form" id="sp-form" novalidate>
        <div class="sp-row"><label>First name<input name="firstname" required autocomplete="given-name"></label><label>Last name<input name="lastname" required autocomplete="family-name"></label></div>
        <div class="sp-row"><label>Email<input name="email" type="email" required autocomplete="email"></label><label>Phone<input name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel"></label></div>
        <div class="sp-row"><label>Organization<input name="company" autocomplete="organization"></label><label>Event website<input name="site" type="url" placeholder="https://"></label></div>
        <div class="sp-row"><label>In person or virtual<select name="mode"><option value="">Choose one</option><option>In person</option><option>Virtual</option><option>Not sure yet</option></select></label><label>Event date(s)<input name="dates" placeholder="e.g. March 12, 2027"></label></div>
        <div class="sp-row"><label>Format<select name="format"><option value="">Choose one</option><option>Keynotes</option><option>Moderated conversations</option><option>Workshops</option><option>Fireside chats</option><option>Leadership offsites</option><option>Guided practices</option><option>Not sure yet</option></select></label><label>Length<select name="length"><option value="">Choose one</option><option>Under 1 hour</option><option>1 to 2 hours</option><option>Half day</option><option>Full day</option><option>Not sure yet</option></select></label></div>
        <div class="sp-row"><label>Topic of interest<select name="topic"><option value="">Choose one</option><option>The Listening Loop</option><option>Trust is a daily deposit</option><option>Yours, or inherited?</option><option>One small thing a day</option><option>Who sings the “we”?</option><option>Law, life, legacy: one house</option><option>Let AI get brilliant. Let us get wiser.</option><option>Whose choice was it?</option><option>Hand on the key</option><option>The films that saw it coming</option><option>Something else</option></select></label><label>Proposed budget<select name="budget"><option value="">Choose one</option><option>Under $5,000</option><option>$5,000 to $10,000</option><option>$10,000 to $20,000</option><option>Over $20,000</option><option>Not sure yet</option></select></label></div>
        <div class="sp-row"><label>Location<input name="location" placeholder="City, state"></label><label>Expected attendance<input name="size" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="e.g. 250"></label></div>
        <label>Who is in the audience, and what do you hope they leave with?<textarea name="about" rows="4"></textarea></label>
        <button class="btn btn-acc" type="submit">Send the request</button>
        <p class="sp-msg" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>
    </div></section>

    <section class="sec dark vid-sec" id="russ"><video class="bgvid" autoplay muted loop playsinline><source src="https://assets.mixkit.co/videos/47818/47818-720.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video><div class="veil"></div><div class="wrap guide-grid">
      <img src="/russ-michaels.jpg" alt="Russ Michaels" width="340" height="425" loading="lazy" />
      <div><p class="eyebrow">About the speaker</p><h2>Russ Michaels, Esq.</h2><p class="lede">Founder of Vault Human. For over twenty years Russ has led organizations as a CEO, executive director and board president, and he still practices law. He speaks as an operator and a builder, not a theorist: someone who has raised capital, run teams, and stood with people through the decisions that shape a life.</p><p class="lede">His SXSW 2027 proposal, “Who Sings the We? Optimized Out of Your Own World,” is on <a href="/sxsw">the SXSW page</a>. Read his thinking in <a href="/writing">Writing</a>.</p><div class="ctarow"><a class="btn btn-acc" href="#book">Book Russ</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/russ-michaels/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a></div></div>
    </div></section>

